> ### Name: bulknull
> ### Title: One-Call Wrapper for Bulk-Null Dilution Diagnostics
> ### Aliases: bulknull
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> # Example: DPP9 in M8 myeloid cells from IPF cohort
> result <- bulknull(
+   bulk_beta = -0.084210,
+   bulk_se = 0.062774,
+   bulk_fdr = 0.449745,
+   sc_zscore = 2.077409,
+   cluster_fraction = 1332 / 19175,
+   condition_fraction = 0.631,
+   n_cluster = 1332,
+   alpha = 0.05,
+   sided = "one"
+ )
> 
> print(result)

=== BULKNULL DIAGNOSTIC RESULT ===

INPUT PARAMETERS:
  Bulk effect (beta):            -0.08421 
  Bulk SE:                       0.062774 
  Bulk FDR:                      0.449745 
  Single-cell z-score:           2.077409 
  Cluster fraction:              0.06946545 
  Condition fraction:            0.631 
  Cluster size (n):              1332 

APPLICABILITY GATE:
  Status:                        PASSED 

COMPUTED STATISTICS:
  mu (dilution):                 0.1305362 
  z (bulk):                      -1.341479 

DILUTION DISCORDANCE SCORE (DDS):
  Value:                         0.4542207 
  Interpretation:                Weak evidence for dilution 
  (>0.7 strong | >0.5 moderate | >0.3 weak | <=0.3 minimal)

DIAGNOSABILITY INDEX (DI):
  Value:                         0.06497268 
  Interpretation:                Low power (underpowered) 
  (<0.3 low power | <0.8 moderate | >=0.8 high power)

VERDICT:
   UNDERPOWERED: Study lacks power to detect dilution; DDS result inconclusive 

